.TH MV 1
.SH NAME
mv \- rename or move a file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mv
.I from to
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mv
is a command built into the shell,
.BR sh (1).
It gives the file or directory
.I from
the name
.IR to ,
in the same directory or another, in one step: nothing is copied.
.I to
is the full new name, not a directory to move into.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0, or 1 on failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cp (1),
.BR ln (1),
.BR sh (1)
.SH BUGS
A file cannot move between volumes (a user's home is one): "not across
volumes". Copy it with
.BR cp (1)
then remove it.
